# index.html contracts

One HtmlService page. Tailwind CDN, Inter, Dew 2.0 type scale (12 / 14 / 18 / 24, weights 400–600), Dew surfaces and brand blue `#276cf0`. `en-IN` currency. No build step. Heat-map fills come from `getHeatmapStyle`. Cells have no border. Corpus and Net Profit use the absolute-return color. NAV, units, and invested stay plain. Percents use `formatPct` (`12.3%`, one decimal, no plus on gains). Table amounts are whole rupees. Matrix figures use IBM Plex Sans at weight 500 with tabular lining figures. Labels stay Inter. Do not use a monospace face for amounts or rates.

## Chrome
- View dropdown in the header, immediately before **Refresh Data**: `matrix` (Return Matrix), `compare` (Fund Comparator), or `risk` (Risk and Rating). Risk cells use the same heat colors. Green is the better end of that ratio, so lower-is-better figures are flipped before coloring.
- Theme control fixed bottom left: Light / Dark / System, stored as `mf-matrix-theme`. `html.dark` swaps Dew tokens. Empty heat cells follow the active theme.
- Page must fit desktop and phone. `overflow-x: hidden` on the page. Below 768px, KPI cards are 2×2, the matrix scrolls inside `.matrix-scroll`, only Fund Name stays frozen, and the group header row is hidden.

## Return Matrix
`allFunds`, `currentDisplayFunds`, `top2FilterActive` (default true), `activeMetric` (`xirr` | `cagr`), sort default `1Y` descending.
Changing SIP amount, SIP day, or dates calls `getFundMatrixData`. Filters, Top 2, sort, and the metric switch stay in the browser.
- Category, AMC, and Scheme are checkbox lists with Select All. Select All applies no restriction. The three lists intersect. Top 2 then keeps two schemes per remaining category by the active 1Y series when the scheme selection is All.
- The matrix toolbar, immediately before Top 2 / Cat, has a fund search. It multi-selects schemes and includes All and None. It writes the same scheme selection as the Scheme filter. All means no scheme restriction, so Top 2 can still narrow the rows. A checked subset is shown as selected. None selects nothing.
- Fund checklists share `fundChecklistHtml`. The matrix search, Fund Comparator, and Risk and Rating all group schemes by category.
- Tenures, in order: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y` `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y`. Groups are Short and Long. Keep columns compact. SIP XIRR hides `5D` and `15D`. Trailing CAGR still shows them.
- The SIP XIRR / Trailing CAGR switch re-renders tenure cells only. Custom Range XIRR, SIP Corpus, Net Profit, and Absolute return do not follow it.
- Every metric column has a sort icon. Nulls sort last.
- Desktop freeze: `#` and Fund Name. There is no Code column. Drag the Fund Name header edge to set its width; the width is stored as `mf-matrix-name-width` and the column stays frozen. Move up is green, move down is red, 1px apart, and exempt from the 32px button height. Up/down reorders the current view only.

## Fund Comparator
User checks funds. Unchecked, the selected funds are one pool, plus the overall leader. **Compare within category** adds the leader of each selected fund’s full category.
Max benefit is the highest `customRangeXirr` for the same SIP (From, To, amount, day). Net profit breaks a tie. Sale Date does not pick the winner. The table always shows the best of the selected funds and the overall leader across every tracked scheme. With **Compare within category** checked, category cards flow side by side. Each card shows the leader of that category’s full list. That leader’s invested amount, corpus, and net profit are multiplied by how many selected funds are in the category, as if every one of those SIPs went into that one fund. Rates stay unscaled.
Comparator and matrix amounts are whole rupees. Percentages keep one decimal and do not prefix a plus on gains. Comparator figures use Source Sans 3 at 11px.
Table columns stay compact: rank, fund, invested, corpus, net profit, absolute, custom XIRR, then `3M` `6M` `1Y` `3Y` `5Y` `10Y` from the active series. There is no category column. The category leader row has a light fill. Other winning marks stay on the rank cell.
